  <constraints>
    <constraint type="cost">Agent step costs approximately $0.03-0.08 per compilation depending on diff size. This is the most expensive sub-step in the COMPILE phase. Model selection impacts cost — sonnet is preferred for cost efficiency.</constraint>
    <constraint type="article-format">Articles MUST follow the Karpathy wiki pattern: YAML frontmatter delimited by --- followed by structured sections (Purpose, Key Exports, Dependencies, Dependents, Signals, Missing Signals, Notes). All frontmatter fields are required.</constraint>
    <constraint type="naming">File naming convention: knowledge/code/{slug}.md where slug replaces path separators with -- (e.g., src/components/auth.tsx becomes src--components--auth.tsx.md). This naming enables bidirectional mapping between source files and wiki articles.</constraint>
    <constraint type="wikilinks">All cross-references MUST use [[wikilinks]] format (e.g., [[code/src--components--auth.tsx]]). Wikilink section placement determines edge type in Memgraph. Dependencies section links become DEPENDS_ON edges.</constraint>
    <constraint type="idempotency">The compiler must be idempotent. Running compilation twice on the same diff should produce the same result. Existing articles should be updated in place, not duplicated.</constraint>
    <constraint type="scope">The compiler ONLY processes files listed in DIFF_MANIFEST. It does not scan the entire codebase. This keeps compilation time proportional to change size.</constraint>
  </constraints>

